  <h1>TIDE: Shrinking Diffusion LLMs 22× Without Losing the Code Superpower</h1>
  <p class="lead">Diffusion language models generate all tokens simultaneously — giving them a structural edge on code, where global coherence matters. The catch: competitive dLLMs need 8–100B parameters. TIDE is the first cross-architecture distillation framework, compressing a 16B MoE teacher into a 0.6B student with 22× less memory and a 16-point HumanEval advantage over same-size autoregressive models.</p>
