    <tr><td>Qwen3-0.6B (AR baseline)</td><td class="mn">0.6B</td><td class="mn">1.2 GB</td><td class="mn">51.3</td><td class="mn">32.3</td></tr>
    <tr><td>BD3LM-0.6B, no distill</td><td class="mn">0.6B</td><td class="mn">1.4 GB</td><td class="mn">42.1</td><td class="mn">46.3</td></tr>
    <tr class="highlight-row"><td>TIDE distilled (best)</td><td class="mn">0.6B</td><td class="mn">1.4 GB</td><td class="mn">41.0</td><td class="mn best">49.4</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Distillation adds only 2.6% throughput overhead over the undistilled BD3LM (41.0 vs 42.1 tok/s), confirming that the quality gains come entirely from training — not from any architectural change that would affect inference.</p>
</section>

